cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "pegRNA: automated pegRNA design for prime editing (template-jumping PE and Prime Assembly)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: MIT
url: "https://pegrna.ukdri.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thepigdestroyer/pegRNA-pipeline"
abstract: >-
  pegRNA is a design pipeline and web tool for prime editing. Given a target gene
  and an insert (a tag, cassette or gene), it designs pegRNAs, nicking guides and,
  for Prime Assembly, the linear donor DNA, and ranks the candidates. It supports
  template-jumping prime editing (tj-PE; Zheng et al. 2023) for inserts up to about
  500 bp, and Prime Assembly (Liu et al. 2026). Each design passes gates for codon
  recoding (every changed nucleotide is reported), RNA folding, cryptic splicing,
  off-target sites, predicted editing efficiency, and structure and docking. It runs
  as a command-line tool and as a web app at https://pegrna.ukdri.org. Designs are
  computational predictions and have not been validated at the bench.
keywords:
  - prime editing
  - pegRNA
  - CRISPR
  - genome editing
  - protein tagging
  - knock-in
  - Prime Assembly
  - template-jumping prime editing
  - iPSC
